# ---------------- Depth 5: the crown's strongroom ----------------

@event bonded_strongroom
title: The Crown's Strongroom
thread: job_bonded
class: story
tone: tense
when: job_depth >= 5
repeat: 1
art: lock
tags: heist money
scene: A heavy iron door with a crown cast on it at the end of a dark warehouse floor, a big padlock, a student kneeling at the lock with a lantern shaded under their coat.
text: {seen(bonded_strongroom) > 1: The strongroom's iron door again, the crown on it, the same padlock.|At the end of the floor, behind an iron door with the crown cast on it, is the customs' strongroom: everything the crown has seized, waiting for auction. The padlock is the size of your two fists.} {flag(bonded_strongroom): You've had it open before.|}
> left: Leave it and get out
  queue job_way_out now
  say: {seen(bonded_strongroom) > 1: You leave the crown its strongroom and go while the round's at the far end.|You leave the iron door alone and go, by the long way, with what you have.}
> right: Work the padlock
  challenge feat using guile adept- +1 if flag(bonded_round_counted):
    win:
      job_loot += 3
      say: {flag(bonded_strongroom): The padlock gives again. Inside, the seized goods have changed, and you fill your coat with the pick of them.|The padlock gives with a sound like a cough. Inside, on shelves: seized jewellery, a case of duelling pistols, bolts of contraband lace, and a drawer nobody has locked. You fill your coat with the best of the jewellery before you look at the drawer.}
      if flag(bonded_ledger):
        queue job_way_out now
      else:
        queue bonded_ledger now
      flag bonded_strongroom
    lose:
      if job_cover > 0:
        queue job_slip now
      else:
        queue job_caught now
      say: {seen(bonded_strongroom) > 1: The padlock won't move, and you work at it too long. The round comes back early.|The pick snaps in the lock, and the iron door booms when you knock it, and a whistle answers.}
> up[item:lockpick_roll]: Pick it with the proper tools
  challenge feat using guile adept- likely:
    win:
      job_loot += 3
      say: {flag(bonded_strongroom): Eleven picks, and you know which one now. The door opens on the crown's newest seizures, and you fill your coat with the best of them.|Eleven picks and a tension wrench, and the padlock opens on the fourth. Inside, on shelves: seized jewellery, a case of duelling pistols, bolts of contraband lace, and a drawer nobody has locked. You fill your coat with the best of the jewellery before you look at the drawer.}
      if flag(bonded_ledger):
        queue job_way_out now
      else:
        queue bonded_ledger now
      flag bonded_strongroom
    lose:
      if job_cover > 0:
        queue job_slip now
      else:
        queue job_caught now
      say: {seen(bonded_strongroom) > 1: Even with the proper picks the old lock fights you, and the round comes back before it gives.|The fourth pick bends, then the fifth, and while you fumble for the sixth a whistle goes at the end of the floor.}

@event bonded_ledger
title: The Foreman's Ledger
trigger: queued
class: story
tone: grim
repeat: 1
art: paper
tags: heist mystery
scene: A student in a dark strongroom reading a ledger by a shaded lantern, two columns of figures in the same hand, a page with a date circled.
text: In the unlocked drawer there's a ledger in the warehouse foreman's hand. Two columns for every cargo: what came in, and what the crown was told came in. The difference goes out by a side door, month after month. One night is circled: a crate gone that the foreman had sold already, {has(origin_street): and Jory caught on the floor that night with nothing in his hands, and sent down for the lot.|and a young man from one of Port Calder's street crews, caught on the floor that night, sent to gaol for the lot.}
> left: Send it to the magistrate
  alignment +small
  say: Before dawn you leave the ledger wrapped in oilcloth on the magistrate's own doorstep, unsigned. Within the week the foreman's in the cells{has(origin_street): and Jory's out of them, blinking at the daylight on the loft step.|, and the young crew boy who took his blame walks out of gaol.} Nobody knows who sent it. You lose the ledger's price, and don't miss it.
  flag bonded_ledger
  flag jory_freed
  queue job_way_out now
> right: Sell it back to the foreman
  gold +medium
  alignment -small
  say: You send the foreman one page of his own ledger and a time. He comes alone, pays in gold without a word, and burns the book in front of you. {has(origin_street): Jory stays where he is.|The crew boy who took his blame stays where he is.} The gold is heavy in your pocket all the way home.
  flag bonded_ledger
  queue job_way_out now

# ---------------- Jory home (the crew's loft, for a Port Calder childhood) ----------------

@event crew_loft_jory_home
title: Jory Home
pool: capital_crew_loft_home
tone: warm
when: flag(jory_freed)
art: bed
scene: A harbour-town loft with a row of hammocks, a thin young man sitting up in one eating soup, a sharp-eyed older woman and a student at the stove, the crew round a card table.
text: {seen(crew_loft_empty_hammock) > 0: The empty hammock isn't empty. Jory's in it, thinner,|There's a face in the loft you know only from the foreman's ledger: Jory, back from a year in the city gaol, in his own hammock, thinner,} with a bowl of soup and the whole loft finding reasons to walk past him. "Somebody sent the magistrate a book," he tells you. "Nobody knows who." Across the stove Nan Merrow looks at you once, and goes back to dealing.
> left: Stand the loft a round
  gold -small
  mood +small
  say: You buy the loft a round, and then another, and Jory tells the whole room about the gaol's food till they beg him to stop. Nan says nothing at all to you all night, which in the loft is the highest thing she has to give.
> right: Sit with Jory a while
  mood +small
  health -tiny
  say: You sit up with Jory by the stove till the small hours, talking about nothing, while he eats everything in reach. In the morning he's asleep in his own hammock for the first time in a year, and you're grey with tiredness.

# ---------------- The house on the Crescent: found, watched and entered (C5b) ----------------
# The tallest house on the Crescent, uptown, where a shipowner who bought his way up the hill gives a ball every week of
# whenever he's in town (a garden ball in summer). In through the gala (job_where 2): band 1 the ballroom (depth 1–2, apprentice),
# band 2 upstairs (3–4, journeyman), depth 5 the safe in the study. Found by a club invitation (club_gala_card) or the
# Undercroft's fence (undercroft_crescent_tip). Cover: 1, +1 with an invitation (crescent_invited), +1 with the
# servants' hour (crescent_servants_hour).

@event club_gala_card
title: An Invitation, Not Yours
pool: capital_club_life
tone: light
weight: 20
when: not flag(crescent_known)
art: letter
scene: A members' club's leather armchair, a stiff gilt-edged invitation card fallen down between the cushions, a student holding it up to the lamp.
text: Down the side of a club armchair, among the crumbs and a lost glove, there's a stiff gilt-edged card: an invitation to a ball at the tallest house on the Crescent, this week and every week he's in town, "and guest". The name on it belongs to a member snoring in the next chair.
> left: Keep it
  alignment -tiny
  say: You put it in your pocket. The member snores on. It's only a card, you tell yourself, and he has a hundred; you feel it in your pocket all the way home, like a stone.
  flag crescent_invited
  flag crescent_known
> right: Wake him and give it back
  mood -tiny
  say: You wake him. He's furious at being woken, then delighted about the card, then furious again, and tells you all about the house: a shipowner's, new money, a safe in the study "the size of a wardrobe", he says, as if that were vulgar. You leave without even a thank-you.
  flag crescent_known

@event undercroft_crescent_tip
title: The Shipowner's Safe
pool: capital_undercroft_life
tone: tense
weight: 20
when: not flag(crescent_known) and seen(undercroft_fence) > 0
art: lock
scene: A fence in a velvet waistcoat in a candlelit cellar alcove, leaning across his table of watches and rings to speak low to a student, a jeweller's loupe in his eye.
text: The fence in the velvet waistcoat beckons you to his alcove. "A word, academy. The tallest house on the Crescent. A shipowner, new money, a ball every week he's in town and a safe in the study that the whole of Port Calder paid for, one way and another." He polishes his loupe. "I'd pay well for anything in it. Only saying."
> left: Ask him how you'd get in
  alignment -tiny
  say: "During the ball," he says, "everybody's somebody. The servants' door's on the mews, and the servants change over at eleven." He doesn't charge for it. That's how you know he means it.
  flag crescent_servants_hour
  flag crescent_known
> right: Say you'll think about it
  mood -tiny
  say: "Do," he says, and smiles, and goes back to his loupe as if you'd already said yes. "Eleven o'clock," he adds, to the watch he's mending. "The mews door." You walk out knowing exactly which house he meant, and that he knows you know, which sits badly with you all night.
  flag crescent_servants_hour
  flag crescent_known

@pool capital_crescent_life
place: capital_crescent_house
class: routine
repeat: 3
weight: 10
tags: social danger

@event crescent_gala_lights
title: The Ball on the Crescent
pool: capital_crescent_life
tone: light
art: candle
scene: A tall lit-up town house on a curving terrace after dark, carriages drawing up, music and figures behind tall windows, a student watching from the railings of the gardens opposite.
text: {seen(crescent_gala_lights) > 1: The ball again, the carriages, the music. A footman on the steps is turning people away, politely, with his whole face, and a linkman with a torch is sitting on the railings beside you, waiting for his gentleman.|The tallest house on the Crescent is lit from cellar to attic. Carriages queue round the curve, {season == "winter": breath steaming from the horses,|the summer air still warm,} and from the tall windows comes music and the noise of money enjoying itself. A linkman with a torch sits on the gardens' railings beside you.}
> left: Count the windows and the doors
  guile +tiny
  health -tiny
  say: You stand at the gardens' railings until you know every window, the mews door, the footmen (too many), and which room upstairs is the study. {season == "winter": Your hands have gone numb and your feet ache.|The midges have had you for supper and your feet ache.}
> right: Pay the linkman for the servants' hour
  gold -tiny
  mood +tiny
  say: {flag(crescent_servants_hour): You give the linkman a coin for his company. He tells you the cook's name and the dog's, and the house's whole week of scandal, and you already know about the mews door at eleven.|You give the linkman a coin for his torch and his gossip. The servants change over at eleven, he says; the mews door stands open for the trays.}
  flag crescent_servants_hour

# The heist's start: after the street's routine card on an evening or night visit (order: last), once a month.
@pool capital_crescent_entry
place: capital_crescent_house
class: routine
repeat: 1
order: last

@event crescent_enter
title: Everybody's Somebody
pool: capital_crescent_entry
tone: tense
art: mask
tags: danger
scene: A student in borrowed evening clothes slipping in through a lit doorway among elegant guests in silks and jewels, a grand staircase and chandeliers inside.
text: {job_crescent_deepest == 0: Tonight the tallest house on the Crescent is giving its ball, and during a ball everybody's somebody. Upstairs, past the ballroom and the guests on the stairs, there's a study with a safe the size of a wardrobe.|{&The ball again, and the music, and the study upstairs.|Carriages at the door, the mews door open for the trays.|The tall house, lit up, and the safe waiting.}} {flag(crescent_invited): You've a gilt card that says "and guest".|You'll need a way in.}
> left: Not tonight
  say: {&You leave the ball to its guests and walk home under the gardens' trees.|Not tonight. The music follows you down the hill.|You watch the carriages a while longer, and go.}
> right: Go in
  hint: A heist: press on card by card, slip away with what you carry any time.
  flag crescent_tried
  job_where = 2
  job_loot = 0
  job_cover = 1
  if flag(crescent_invited):
    job_cover += 1
  if flag(crescent_servants_hour):
    job_cover += 1
  job_depth = 1
  queue any in job_crescent now
  say: {flag(crescent_invited): You hand the footman your gilt card, and he bows you in under the chandeliers as somebody's guest.|{flag(crescent_servants_hour): At eleven you go in by the mews door behind a tray of ices, as if you'd carried one all your life.|You go in on the tail of a noisy party from a carriage, laughing at nothing, as if you belonged to it.}}

@thread job_crescent
from: scene
name: The house on the Crescent
premise: The tallest house on the Crescent gives a ball every week its owner is in town, and has a safe in the study the size of a wardrobe.
journal:
  flag(crescent_tried): You went into the ball on the Crescent, to rob it.
  flag(crescent_letters): In the shipowner's writing desk you read his letters to a warehouse foreman on the wharf.
  flag(crescent_safe): You opened the safe in the shipowner's study.
status:
  resolved: flag(crescent_safe)

@event crescent_dead_end
title: The Music Stops
thread: job_crescent
class: routine
tone: tense
when: job_depth >= 1 and (job_depth <= 4 or (seen(crescent_safe_card) > 0 and since(crescent_safe_card) == 0))
repeat: 1
weight: 1
art: mask
tags: heist
scene: A grand staircase in a lit town house, a stern butler standing at the top of it with his hands behind his back, a student halfway up in evening clothes.
text: {job_depth >= 5: The safe has had all the listening it'll bear tonight, and somebody's coming up the stairs with a lamp. The only way left is down.|{&The butler has taken up a post at the top of the stairs and isn't moving. The only way that's still a way is down.|The music stops for a speech, and every face in the house turns your way. Not tonight.|A door along the landing is locked, and voices behind the next one. Whatever's further on isn't for tonight.}}
> left: Go with what you carry
  queue job_way_out now
  say: {job_depth >= 5: You leave the safe and go down the back stairs with what you have.|{&You turn and go down among the guests, and out with a crowd that's leaving.|You take the hint, and your coat, and go.|You go down the back stairs, past a maid who doesn't look up.}}
> right: Look about where you stand
  challenge deceive apprentice:
    win:
      job_loot += 1
      say: {job_depth >= 5: On the study's mantel there's a little gold snuffbox nobody will count tonight. It comes with you.|{&On a side table a guest has left a gold cigar case. It comes with you.|In the crush a pearl drops from somebody's earring. You pick it up, and keep it.|A silver card tray, with nobody's eye on it. It comes with you.}}
    lose:
      mood -tiny
      say: {job_depth >= 5: A maid comes in to see to the fire, and you have to admire the clock for a long minute, and leave empty-handed.|{&A footman watches your hands the whole time. You leave them in your pockets.|A guest catches your eye and keeps it. You smile, and touch nothing.|You find nothing worth the risk, and a dowager's stare.}}
  queue job_way_out now

# ---------------- Band 1: the ballroom (depth 1–2, apprentice) ----------------

@event crescent1_footman
title: The Footman's Eye
thread: job_crescent
class: routine
tone: tense
when: job_depth >= 1 and job_depth <= 2
repeat: 1
art: mask
tags: heist danger
scene: A tall footman in powdered wig and livery at the door of a ballroom, looking down his nose at a student in evening clothes, dancers whirling beyond.
text: {seen(crescent1_footman) > 1: The same footman at the ballroom doors, the same moment too long.|At the ballroom doors, past the hall, a footman in a powdered wig looks at every guest as they pass, and at you a moment longer.}
> left: Back out into the night
  queue job_way_out now
  say: {seen(crescent1_footman) > 1: You leave the footman to his doors and go home.|You turn back as if you'd forgotten your gloves, and keep going, out of the house.}
> right: Look as if you belong
  challenge deceive apprentice +1 if flag(crescent_invited):
    win:
      job_depth += 1
      next
      say: {seen(crescent1_footman) > 1: You walk past him talking over your shoulder to nobody about the terrible music. He bows you through.|You give him the faint, bored smile of somebody who has been to a great many of these. He bows, slightly. You're in.}
    lose:
      if job_cover > 0:
        queue job_slip now
      else:
        queue job_caught now
      say: {seen(crescent1_footman) > 1: He steps across the doorway, very politely, and doesn't step back.|"Your name, sir or madam?" he asks, in a voice that carries.}
> up[glamour]: Charm him
  job_depth += 1
  next
  say: {seen(crescent1_footman) > 1: He remembers liking you, and not quite why. He bows.|You smile at him with a little more charm than you have, and he finds himself remembering you from last week. He bows you in.}

@event crescent1_quadrille
title: A Partner for the Quadrille
thread: job_crescent
class: routine
tone: light
when: job_depth >= 1 and job_depth <= 2
repeat: 1
art: heart
tags: heist social
