  next
  say: {seen(crescent1_conservatory) > 1: Up the iron stair, quiet as you can on iron, and out behind the curtain.|You go up the little iron stair among the hanging ferns, and come out on the upper floor behind a curtain.}

# ---------------- Band 2: upstairs (depth 3–4, journeyman) ----------------

@event crescent2_back_stairs
title: The Back Stairs
thread: job_crescent
class: routine
tone: tense
when: job_depth >= 3 and job_depth <= 4
repeat: 1
art: meal
tags: heist danger
scene: A narrow servants' staircase in a grand house, maids and footmen hurrying up and down with trays, a student in evening clothes carrying a tray among them.
text: {seen(crescent2_back_stairs) > 1: The back stairs, busier than ever. Somebody's left a full tray on the landing.|The back stairs, where the servants run: trays going up, trays coming down, a cook shouting from below. The study is at the top.} {flag(crescent_servants_hour): The eleven o'clock changeover is still going on, and nobody is sure who should be where.|}
> left: Go down and out by the mews
  queue job_way_out now
  say: {seen(crescent2_back_stairs) > 1: You slip down the back stairs and out into the mews, and breathe.|You go down with the empty trays and out by the mews door.}
> right: Carry a tray up
  challenge deceive journeyman +1 if flag(crescent_servants_hour):
    win:
      job_depth += 1
      next
      say: {seen(crescent2_back_stairs) > 1: You go up with a tray of ices, and the housekeeper herself holds the door for you.|You pick up a tray of glasses and go up with the others, eyes down. Nobody looks at a tray.}
    lose:
      if job_cover > 0:
        queue job_slip now
      else:
        queue job_caught now
      say: {seen(crescent2_back_stairs) > 1: You hold the tray like a guest, not a servant, and a footman sees it at once.|The housekeeper stops you on the stair. "I don't know you," she says, and takes the tray.}

@event crescent2_lapdog
title: The Lapdog
thread: job_crescent
class: routine
tone: light
when: job_depth >= 3 and job_depth <= 4
repeat: 1
art: paw
tags: heist danger
scene: A small fat pug with a jewelled collar standing in the middle of a grand upstairs corridor, about to bark, a student crouching with a biscuit held out.
text: {seen(crescent2_lapdog) > 1: The lapdog again, in the corridor, in its collar. It remembers you, and it's taking a breath.|In the middle of the upstairs corridor stands a small, fat dog in a jewelled collar, and it's taking a deep breath.}
> left: Back away before it barks
  queue job_way_out now
  say: {seen(crescent2_lapdog) > 1: You leave the dog the corridor. It seems to expect nothing less.|You back away, very slowly, and go down and out.}
> right: Make friends, fast
  challenge soothe journeyman:
    win:
      job_depth += 1
      next
      say: {seen(crescent2_lapdog) > 1: You crouch and find the right ear, and it rolls over before you've finished.|You crouch, hold out a hand, and scratch exactly the right place behind its ear. It sighs and rolls over. You step over it.}
    lose:
      if job_cover > 0:
        queue job_slip now
      else:
        queue job_caught now
      say: {seen(crescent2_lapdog) > 1: It goes for your ankle and holds on, yapping, and won't be shaken off.|It barks: a high, endless, carrying bark. Doors open all along the corridor.}
> up[sleight]: Palm it a biscuit from the supper table
  job_depth += 1
  next
  say: {seen(crescent2_lapdog) > 1: A sugared almond appears under its nose. It forgets the corridor, the house and you.|A biscuit walks out of your sleeve and into its mouth, and the dog forgets you exist.}

@event crescent2_dressing_room
title: The Dressing Room
thread: job_crescent
class: routine
tone: tense
when: job_depth >= 3 and job_depth <= 4
repeat: 1
art: mirror
tags: heist money
scene: A lady's dressing room in a grand house at night, a dressing table with an open jewel case before a tall mirror, a portrait on the wall, a student reaching for a necklace.
text: {seen(crescent2_dressing_room) > 1: The dressing room again, the jewel case open again. She changes her mind every week.|A dressing room, lamp left lit: a dressing table, a tall mirror, and an open jewel case, the lady of the house having changed her mind about her necklace at the last minute. A portrait of her watches from the wall.}
> left: Leave the jewels and go
  queue job_way_out now
  say: {seen(crescent2_dressing_room) > 1: You leave her her necklaces and slip back down.|You close the jewel case, for some reason, and go.}
> right: Take what she didn't wear
  mood -tiny
  job_loot += 2
  job_depth += 1
  next
  say: {seen(crescent2_dressing_room) > 1: You take a pair of earrings, and don't look in the mirror at all.|You take the necklace she didn't choose. The portrait's eyes follow you to the door, and your own face in the mirror isn't one you like much.}

@event crescent2_writing_desk
title: The Writing Desk
thread: job_crescent
class: routine
tone: eerie
when: job_depth >= 3 and job_depth <= 4
repeat: 1
art: letter
tags: heist mystery
scene: A shipowner's writing desk in a dark panelled room, a bundle of letters tied with tape, a student reading one by a shaded candle.
text: {seen(crescent2_writing_desk) > 1: {flag(jory_freed): The writing desk again. No new letters in the cramped hand: its writer is in the cells, and the shipowner's other correspondents are more careful.|The writing desk again. Another bundle has joined the first, in the same cramped hand.}|In a small panelled room off the landing there's a writing desk, unlocked, with a bundle of letters tied in red tape. The top one is in a cramped hand, and starts "The usual, by the side door, Thursday."} {flag(bonded_ledger): You've seen that hand before, in a ledger in a strongroom.|}
> left: Leave the letters and go
  queue job_way_out now
  say: {seen(crescent2_writing_desk) > 1: You leave the desk to its secrets and slip away.|You put the letters back exactly as they were and go.}
> right: Read them, and keep one
  challenge research journeyman:
    win:
      job_loot += 1
      job_depth += 1
      next
      say: {flag(crescent_letters): {flag(jory_freed): You read what's left of the old bundle for anything you missed, and keep a letter that names a ship. Somebody would pay for it.|You read the new bundle. Same foreman, same side door, a bigger cargo. You keep one, and go on.}|It comes clear as you read: the warehouse foreman on the wharf, two sets of figures, and everything the side door let out came up the hill to this house. Tucked among them, a note in the shipowner's own hand reminds him of his safe's number: his first ship's launching day. You keep the best letter. Somebody would pay for it.}
      flag crescent_letters
    lose:
      if job_cover > 0:
        queue job_slip now
      else:
        queue job_caught now
      say: {seen(crescent2_writing_desk) > 1: The candle gutters over a letter and catches it. The smell of burning paper goes straight down the stairs.|You read too long, and the door opens on a maid with a coal scuttle, who screams.}

@event crescent2_balcony
title: The Balcony Ledge
thread: job_crescent
class: routine
tone: tense
when: job_depth >= 3 and job_depth <= 4
repeat: 1
art: tower
tags: heist danger
scene: A narrow stone ledge running along the outside of a grand town house at night, between two balconies, the lit Crescent and the dark gardens far below, a student edging along it.
text: {seen(crescent2_balcony) > 1: The ledge again, three storeys up. The gardens look darker than last time.|The landing ahead is full of guests' voices, but the next room's balcony is a few yards along the outside wall, and between the two runs a ledge the width of a hand, three storeys up over the Crescent.}
> left: Stay inside and go back down
  queue job_way_out now
  say: {seen(crescent2_balcony) > 1: Not tonight. You go back down among the guests.|You look at the ledge, and at the drop, and go home by the stairs.}
> right: Go along the ledge
  challenge feat journeyman:
    win:
      job_depth += 1
      next
      say: {seen(crescent2_balcony) > 1: You cross without looking down once, until you're over the rail.|You go along the ledge with your back to the house and your heels over the Crescent, and climb over the next balcony's rail into a dark bedroom, shaking.}
    lose:
      if job_cover > 0:
        queue job_slip now
      else:
        queue job_caught now
      say: {seen(crescent2_balcony) > 1: You knock a flowerpot off the ledge. It lands on a carriage roof in front of the whole Crescent.|Your foot goes, and you hang by a drainpipe until somebody in the street below points and shouts.}
> up[shadowstep]: Step from shadow to shadow
  job_depth += 1
  next
  say: {seen(crescent2_balcony) > 1: Shadow to shadow, three storeys up. Your stomach stays behind for a moment.|You step into the shadow of one balcony and out of the next one's, never touching the ledge at all.}

# ---------------- Depth 5: the safe in the study ----------------

@event crescent_safe_card
title: The Safe in the Study
thread: job_crescent
class: story
tone: tense
when: job_depth >= 5
repeat: 1
art: lock
tags: heist money
scene: A shipowner's dark study, a huge green iron safe the size of a wardrobe with a brass dial, a student kneeling with an ear pressed to it, ballroom music faint below.
text: {seen(crescent_safe_card) > 1: The study, the wardrobe of a safe, the brass dial.|The study, at last: ships in bottles, a globe, and in the corner a green iron safe the size of a wardrobe, with a brass dial. Below, the ball goes on. Somewhere in that safe the whole of Port Calder paid for something.} {flag(crescent_safe): You've had it open before.|}
> left: Leave it and go
  queue job_way_out now
  say: {seen(crescent_safe_card) > 1: You leave the dial where it is and go down the back stairs with what you have.|You look at the safe a long time, and decide it isn't tonight, and go.}
> right: Listen to the dial
  challenge feat using guile adept- +1 if flag(crescent_letters):
    win:
      job_loot += 3
      say: {flag(crescent_safe): The tumblers fall for you again. The safe has been refilled since; the shipowner has had a good season.|{flag(crescent_letters): You start from the launching day the shipowner's note let slip, and turn the dial with your ear to the iron until the tumblers fall, one, two, three, four.|You turn the dial with your ear to the iron until the tumblers fall, one, two, three, four.} The door swings out, heavy as a ship's. Inside: bearer bonds, a rope of pearls and a cash box. You take what you can carry.}
      flag crescent_safe
      queue job_way_out now
    lose:
      if job_cover > 0:
        queue job_slip now
      else:
        queue job_caught now
      say: {seen(crescent_safe_card) > 1: You lose the count, start again, lose it again, and somebody tries the door handle.|The dial clicks, and clicks, and tells you nothing, and the study door opens.}
> up[foresight]: See the number before you turn it
  challenge spell adept- likely:
    win:
      job_loot += 3
      say: {flag(crescent_safe): You let Foresight run a breath ahead again, and the door swings out on a refilled safe.|You let Foresight run a few moments ahead and watch yourself open the safe, and then do what you watched. Bearer bonds, a rope of pearls, a cash box. You take what you can carry.}
      flag crescent_safe
      queue job_way_out now
    lose:
      if job_cover > 0:
        queue job_slip now
      else:
        queue job_caught now
      say: {seen(crescent_safe_card) > 1: What Foresight shows you is the study door opening, a moment before it does.|The moments ahead blur into music and footsteps, and the one you see clearest is a footman in the doorway. Then he's there.}
